    skos:definition "a distillation from light-coloured wines and the skins of grapes, manufactured chiefly in the South of Europe; the trade in this spirit being very large. Cognac is the purest, oldest, and palest brandy. British brandy is a cheaper compound of rectified spirits. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 61]"@en ;
