<id/04/0483/#concept> a crm:E55_Type, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Confectionery"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_sugars_sweeteners/#concept> ;
    skos:closeMatch aat:300389830 ;
    skos:definition "(Lat. bellaria; Fr. bonbons; Ital. confitura; Span. confitura; Germ. confect). Sweetmeats. In 1866 we imported 1,135,681 lbs. of foreign confectionery, valued at 42,588*l.*, of which 231,019 lbs. were entered for home consumption, while we exported 1,850,992 lbs. of British and 956,109 lbs. of foreign confectionery; the whole being valued at 118,406*l.* Australia was our chief market. For an account of the confectionery of the ancients we refer the reader to Apicius; and as an authority on the sweetmeats of the old English we would cite Warner's *Antiquitates Culinarie*. [J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 483]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q5159627 ;
