<id/13/1311/#concept> a crm:E55_Type, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Sugar Other Sorts including Sugar Candy"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch aat:300183931, wd:Q11002 ;
    skos:broader <id/sub/sub_sugars_swe_wd_q11002/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "the saccharine constituent of vegetable and animal products. The sugars of commerce are obtained chiefly from the juice of the sugar-cane, the beet-root, the sap of the sugar-maple, and from some of the palms. The following figures show the quantity in cwts. of raw cane sugar consumed in this country within the last four years:— [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 378]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated fields — bridge_1866 set_relation: Species-specific or qualified heading is narrower than the 1866 concept (consistent with sibling headings)."@en ;
